* wizfast - switch the module and the FPGA UART to 921600 baud.
* Needs: wizi, no connections active. Sets the module (AT+UART_CUR) first, then the
* driver: bau=1 on /wz sets the speed bit in the control register; bau=9 on /wz0-/wz3
* is the same bit plus the packet flag (bit 3) those descriptors must keep.
* Undo with wizslow. The setting is lost when the module resets.
echo * WizFi360 Helper - Fast mode
echo ATE1>/wz
modem /wz
echo AT+UART_CUR=921600,8,1,0,0>/wz
modem /wz
xmode /wz bau=1
xmode /wz0 bau=9
xmode /wz1 bau=9
xmode /wz2 bau=9
xmode /wz3 bau=9
echo AT>/wz
modem /wz
